        1→# just-the-docs-template
        3→This is a *bare-minimum* template to create a [Jekyll] site that:
        5→- uses the [Just the Docs] theme;
        6→- can be built and published on [GitHub Pages];
        7→- can be built and previewed locally, and published on other platforms.
        9→More specifically, the created site:
        11→- uses a gem-based approach, i.e. uses a `Gemfile` and loads the `just-the-docs` gem;
        12→- uses the [GitHub Pages / Actions workflow] to build and publish the site on GitHub Pages.
        14→To get started with creating a site, simply:
        16→1. click "[use this template]" to create a GitHub repository
        17→2. go to Settings > Pages > Build and deployment > Source, and select GitHub Actions
        19→If you want to maintain your docs in the `docs` directory of an existing project repo, see [Hosting your docs from an existing project repo](#hosting-your-docs-from-an-existing-project-repo).
        21→After completing the creation of your new site on GitHub, update it as needed:
        23→## Replace the content of the template pages
        …
        25→Update the following files to your own content:
        27→- `index.md` (your new home page)
        28→- `README.md` (information for those who access your site repo on GitHub)
        30→## Changing the version of the theme and/or Jekyll
        …
        32→Simply edit the relevant line(s) in the `Gemfile`.
        34→## Adding a plugin
        …
        55→## Publishing your site on GitHub Pages
        …
        76→## Building and previewing your site locally
        …
        88→## Publishing your built site on a different platform
        …
        90→Just upload all the files in the directory `_site`.
        92→## Customization
        …
        94→You're free to customize sites that you create with this template, however you like!
        96→[Browse our documentation][Just the Docs] to learn more about how to use this theme.
